`,s.jsxs(i.p,{children:["After wrapping up badges, I also started implementing recurring transactions; a feature that's been on my list for a while. These transactions are ideal for subscriptions, letting users skip manual entry for regular payments. Through some research, I learned that RRULE (used by calendar apps for event recurrence) was the best way to handle this. RRULE encodes frequency, intervals, and start/end dates in one string, which then gets stored as the recurrence options for an event. I found ",s.jsx(i.a,{href:"https://github.com/jkbrzt/rrule",children:"this library"})," for constructing RRULE objects so I can calculate transaction dates. I added a table and new functions in DatabaseService for recurring transactions, and then worked on the UI.​"]}),`
