`,s.jsx(i.p,{children:"On the UI side, we’ll be using Jetpack Compose, which is a declarative UI framework similar to React. Both frameworks use functions to build the UI: React has components, while Compose has composables. They also both use state to track changes in the UI and re-render specific elements when needed. Instead of returning HTML tags like in React, Compose uses functions for everything; even elements on screen like buttons and text are functions. Another key difference is styling: React uses CSS, while Compose uses modifiers to handle layout and styles."}),`
